※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4464

※ The asterism says that several things stand where one is written, and only a
※ tuple is several things.  Anything else is one argument already, so there is
※ nothing for the glyph to do and no reading of it that would be an improvement
※ over saying so.

fn one(a: u8) → u8:
    a

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = 7u8
    one(⁂n)
